<!--Render Target Documentation — TargetRegistration
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.TargetRegistration-->
<rdoc:TargetRegistration xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Registry name and how a host constructs the target
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Registry / CLI target name: machineblocks-v3-scad
    npm package: @machineblocks/render-target
    TypeScript class (when implemented): MachineBlocksRenderTarget

    Host wiring:

        import { registerTarget } from "@blockml/compiler";
        import { BlockRenderEngine } from "@blockml/block-render-engine";
        import { MachineBlocksRenderTarget } from "@machineblocks/render-target";

        registerTarget(new MachineBlocksRenderTarget(new BlockRenderEngine()));

    Shape:

        class MachineBlocksRenderTarget implements RenderTarget {
          name = "machineblocks-v3-scad"
          engine = new BlockRenderEngine()
          processors = [
            new ScadSetProcessor(),
            new ScadBlockProcessor()
          ]
          delegates = []
        }

    Both V1 processors use the engine compile strategy.
    delegates stays empty. Other domain targets may list this target as a
    delegate and ship no processors of their own.

    @blockml/cli does not register this name. @machineblocks/cli does.
    Tests and browser callers call registerTarget directly.

    Stage-3 RenderTarget also carries accepts scopes
    (document, library, corpus, auto) and render(request, ctx). This product
    target is a document target: one BML file in, one or more SCAD files out.
    The host requires a file argument unless --all loops srcDir.

    render finds the BomDocument whose source.filePath equals the session
    sourceFilePath. No match returns files: [] and diagnostic
    BML_RENDER_DOCUMENT_NOT_FOUND.

    targetOptions.machineblocks-v3-scad carries mbLibPath and settingsFormat
    (pseudo-map or object).

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:RendererPipeline" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:TargetRegistration>
